mbedded":true},{"title":"called it off amid public opposition","target":"https://valleylookout.com/2025/07/24/chemicals-or-bust-state-punts-on-payette-lake-milfoil-amid-public-opposition-to-herbicide/","line":88},{"title":"St. Luke's Health Plan - 2026 2:1","target":"https://static-v2.boisedev.com/assets/3cffa70b-bd30-43bc-8a9e-62008bbc7dff.png","line":92,"embedded":true},{"title":"St. Luke's Health Plan - 2026 2:1","target":"https://static-v2.boisedev.com/assets/3cffa70b-bd30-43bc-8a9e-62008bbc7dff.png","line":102,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"State adopts milfoil plan as Valley Co. resumes diver removal","source":"https://valleylookout.com/2026/06/05/state-adopts-milfoil-plan-as-valley-co-resumes-diver-removal/","author":["[[Drew Dodson - Valley Lookout Editor]]"],"published":"2026-06-05","created":"2026-07-08","description":"Herbicides will be used in Payette Lake for the first time this summer to kill Eurasian watermilfoil.  The Idaho State Department of Agriculture recently approved a five-year management plan that calls for the use of herbicides as well as mechanical removal by divers to reduce the invasive plant infestation to “manageable levels.”   The plan was […]"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},